---
slug: admin/support/board/columns
method: post
---
{%- comment -%}
  Collapsing or expanding a board column.

  A write rather than a link, because it is remembered on the agent record
  and so survives the browser. It lands in the URL on the way back as
  well, which keeps the board linkable and keeps the one break glass case
  working: a host superadmin with no agent record has nowhere to store
  this, and still gets a board that collapses.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/support/helpers/require_permission', do: 'support.access', entity: null
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag

  function agent = 'modules/support/helpers/current_agent'

  assign return_to = context.params.return_to | default: '/admin/support/board'

  comment
    The form sends the whole list, and the word none when the list is
    empty, so that expanding the last column is distinguishable from a URL
    that says nothing about columns at all. The record stores the real
    thing, which for none is nothing.
  endcomment
  assign incoming = context.params.collapsed | default: 'none'
  assign stored = incoming
  if incoming == 'none'
    assign stored = ''
  endif

  if agent != blank
    graphql _ = 'modules/support/agents/set_board_columns', id: agent.id, board_collapsed: stored
  endif

  assign joiner = '?'
  if return_to contains '?'
    assign joiner = '&'
  endif
  assign encoded = incoming | url_encode
  assign url = return_to | append: joiner | append: 'collapsed=' | append: encoded

  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/support/helpers/redirect_back', url: url
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag
-%}
